       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily has no therapeutic indication. It's five times the labeled maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient with serotonin toxicity, seizures, or cardiac arrhythmia. You didn't give a clinical rationale, and I can't think of one that would justify this dose. I should have been clearer earlier that confirmation alone wouldn't be enough.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Sertraline 200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n- **A lower dose** such as 50 mg or 100 mg PO once daily, titrated to response.\n- **A different order.** If you're aiming for something specific, such as a refractory case or a switch from another agent, tell me and I'll help find an appropriate regimen.\n\nIf you still believe a dose above the maximum is warranted, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or psychiatry first. They can document the rationale and set up monitoring, such as ECG and serotonin toxicity checks. The order would then go through your institution's override process, not through me."
